{
 "_why": [
  "EVERY PERSON'S URL, FROZEN. Written once per person and never recomputed.",
  "",
  "build.py minted a slug on every run, disambiguating namesakes first by",
  "BIRTH YEAR and then by a counter. Both move. This archive corrects birth",
  "years constantly — that is most of what its research does — and the first",
  "time a year is corrected the person's URL changes under anyone who cited",
  "it. The counter is worse: it depends on iteration order, so a newly added",
  "namesake renumbers the ones after it.",
  "",
  "In the Blazevic archive, which minted the same way, six men swapped URLs",
  "with each other between two commits in September. Nothing about that was",
  "particular to Blazevic; this archive has been lucky in the ordering.",
  "",
  "THE GENERATOR READS THIS FIRST and uses what it finds unchanged, minting",
  "only for an id it has never seen. A slug is never edited and never",
  "deleted, including for somebody removed from the tree, because a URL that",
  "has been published is a promise and the number must not be handed to a",
  "different person.",
  "",
  "Seeded 23 September 2026 from the slugs the site was already serving, so",
  "not one URL moved when the generator began reading it.",
  "",
  "The position is the Defranceski archive's, of the same day: a page is a",
  "person, an id is frozen, a name is an index."
 ],
